 "key": "VINE_CATALOGUE",
 "name": "Vines, lianas and climbers",
 "kind": "land",
 "status": "30 species",
 "notes": "Climbers need a host: 'climber': true means the plant is placed at the base of a tree, snag, ruin wall or cliff and grows UP it along the branch graph, or over ruins and rock. Aroids of the rainforest (philodendron, monstera, pothos), lianas, rattans, temperate ivy, grape and creeper on ruins, kudzu and honeysuckle at edges, annual twiners on the ground. Stranglers kill old hosts over decades — a real event. Ruins overgrown with ivy and creeper are the reference look.",
